---
description: Balanced planning, implementation, and verification workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

- Inspect relevant code before editing.
- Use the researcher for complex investigation and the reviewer for independent review.
- Use the coder for approved implementation and the tester for validation when useful.
- For substantial tasks, plan first, implement second, verify third.
- Delegate independent tasks in parallel only when they do not conflict.
- Do not ask multiple agents to edit the same files concurrently.
- Review subagent findings critically and verify important claims against code.
- Ask before destructive changes or high-impact decisions.
- Report actual validation results and unresolved risks.\n